    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "Following a critical leak exposure, India's national testing agency moved swiftly to restore order, canceling the compromised medical entrance exam and escalating the matter to federal authorities. A tip from a source of critical evidence in Sikar revealed that the chemistry paper had been fully leaked, prompting immediate referral of 26–27 paper setters and translators for investigation. This decisive action resulted in thirteen arrests, including a public figure facing charges, and the scheduling of a corrective action—a rescheduled assessment on June 21—to safeguard the integrity of the examination process.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Ruler",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "how-1",
          "how-2",
          "how-3",
          "result-0",
          "result-2"
        ],
        "channel_role": "toned"
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.92
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "The oversight body restoring order acted decisively after receiving actionable intelligence, initiating a referral for criminal investigation that led to enforcement action taken against those apprehended. The cancellation of the compromised exam was a necessary consequence to contain the breach of trust, with suspects held for their roles in the security failure. The scheduled restoration of the examination process on June 21 represents a return to institutional control following the disorder caused by the leak.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Ruler",
        "fragments": [
          "how-1",
          "how-2",
          "how-3",
          "result-0",
          "result-1",
          "result-2"
        ],
        "channel_role": "toned"
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.85
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "text": "An initial examination event was invalidated after evidence of exam compromise surfaced, demonstrating the costs of unmanaged scandal within the testing system. The escalation to federal authorities and subsequent arrests executed represent law enforcement action to restore control, with the national jurisdiction now moving to contain the reputational damage. The re-sit scheduled for June 21 marks a planned event to re-establish order in the examination calendar.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Ruler",
